{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2138-06-26 18:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, Mr. ___. I'm Dr. ___, one of your doctors here. I understand you had trouble breathing earlier today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2138-06-26 18:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I suddenly couldn’t catch my breath and turned blue. I called ___ and they sent an ambulance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2138-06-26 18:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That must have been scary. You were given oxygen and breathing treatments at the other hospital, and your breathing improved. We’re keeping you here to monitor you and figure out what caused this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2138-06-26 18:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had this before. It’s because of the narrowing in my airway from my condition. I have that Ruvalcaba-Myhre-Smith syndrome and relapsing polychondritis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2138-06-26 18:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, I see that. Those conditions can cause scarring and narrowing in your trachea and bronchi. Your oxygen level was low when you arrived, so we’ve put you on extra oxygen through your trach mask."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2138-06-26 18:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That feels better already. But will I need another balloon procedure again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2138-06-26 18:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning for that. Interventional pulmonology will see you tomorrow and likely do a bronchoscopy to check the airway and possibly dilate it again if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2138-06-26 18:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I remember that from last time. It helped, but it comes back."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2138-06-26 18:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it can be recurrent. We’ll manage it step by step. We also checked your blood, and your white blood cell count is high, which can happen with inflammation or infection, but we don’t think it’s an infection right now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2138-06-26 18:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t had a fever or cough. Could it be from my steroids?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2138-06-26 18:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. Chronic steroid use can raise your white count. We’ll watch it. Your chest X-ray didn’t show pneumonia, so that’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2138-06-27 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I reviewed your bronchoscopy schedule — it’s set for 12 PM today. The team will look into your airway and open any tight spots with a balloon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2138-06-27 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be asleep? I was awake last time and it was uncomfortable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2138-06-27 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be under sedation this time, so you’ll be comfortable. Afterward, we’ll keep you here for monitoring and pain control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2138-06-27 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And my potassium was high yesterday — is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2138-06-27 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it was slightly high on admission but came down. We’ll keep an eye on it, but it’s not concerning now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2138-06-27 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back. How are you feeling after the procedure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2138-06-27 13:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Tired, but my breathing feels easier already. Was it successful?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2138-06-27 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. They found significant narrowing in your trachea and both main bronchi. They used balloons to open them up — your left main stem and trachea were dilated successfully."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2138-06-27 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried it might be worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2138-06-27 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also took some washings from your airway to check for infection. Results aren’t back yet, but we’ll follow up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2138-06-27 13:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I haven’t been using my tobramycin nebulizer. I didn’t have a nebulizer at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2138-06-27 13:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Ah, that’s important. You have chronic Pseudomonas colonization, and that nebulizer helps keep your lungs clear. Infectious disease recommends restarting it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2138-06-27 13:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t realize it was that important. Can I get a nebulizer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2138-06-27 13:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll send one home with you, along with the tobramycin prescription. It’s key to preventing flare-ups."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2138-06-27 13:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll use it. What about my Esbriet? I stopped that too — it was giving me stomach upset."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2138-06-27 13:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We know. Your GERD symptoms may be from Esbriet. We’ve kept your famotidine twice daily, which should help. Please restart Esbriet with meals — it’s important for your lung health."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2138-06-27 13:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try. And my chest pain — is that related?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2138-06-27 13:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your ECG showed some changes, but they look chronic — not new heart damage. Your troponins were negative. It’s likely related to your connective tissue disease, not your heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2138-06-27 13:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I only take oxycodone occasionally for it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2138-06-27 13:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep it available for pain. You’re on 10 mg every 6 hours as needed, and it’s working well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2138-06-28 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs this morning look much better. Your white count has dropped from 18 to 8.9 — that’s a good sign of reduced inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2138-06-28 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. And my breathing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2138-06-28 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on room air now through your trach mask and saturating at 100%. No more desaturations. The bronchoscopy really helped."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2138-06-28 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel stronger. When can I go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2138-06-28 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly tomorrow. We want to make sure you’re stable and have all your prescriptions ready, especially the nebulizer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2138-06-29 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, we’re clearing you for discharge today. Your breathing is stable, labs are good, and you’re feeling much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2138-06-29 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good news. What do I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2138-06-29 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue all your medications — especially the tobramycin nebulizer and Esbriet with food. Use the oxycodone only if you have pain. And follow up with pulmonology in one month for another bronchoscopy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2138-06-29 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if I start having trouble breathing again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2138-06-29 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your doctor or go to the ER. We’ve also given you a Narcan spray in case of accidental overdose — keep it handy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2138-06-29 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thank you — I feel ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2138-06-29 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2138-06-29 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing — the bronchial washings. What if they find something?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2138-06-29 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’re still pending, but even so, we’re continuing the tobramycin because of your history. If anything urgent comes up, your doctor will call you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2138-06-29 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes me feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2138-06-29 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming — you have your nebulizer, medications, and follow-up appointments scheduled?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2138-06-29 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, everything’s here. I’ll start the nebulizer tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2138-06-29 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. And remember, your condition needs consistent care. Staying on your meds helps prevent these hospital visits."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2138-06-29 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I understand. I’ll do better with adherence."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2138-06-29 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s all we ask. Take care, Mr. ___."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2138-06-29 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2138-06-29 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Quick update — your discharge papers are ready. You’re cleared to leave whenever you’re ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2138-06-29 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I’ll get my things together."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2138-06-29 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final check — any chest pain or breathing issues since this morning?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2138-06-29 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "None. I feel steady."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2138-06-29 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. You’re doing well. Safe travels home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2138-06-29 13:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2138-06-29 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing — your rheumatology follow-up is scheduled. Keep taking your prednisone and losartan as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2138-06-29 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. I’ll see you all in a month."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2138-06-26 18:14:00",
    "admission_end": "2138-06-29 17:19:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted for acute hypoxemic respiratory failure due to recurrent tracheal and bronchial stenosis from Ruvalcaba-Myhre-Smith syndrome and relapsing polychondritis. He presented with sudden shortness of breath and cyanosis at home, requiring EMS transport. He was stabilized with oxygen and nebulizers, then underwent bronchoscopy with balloon dilation of the trachea and bilateral mainstem bronchi, which improved his airway patency and oxygenation. His leukocytosis resolved without antibiotics, and pain was managed with oxycodone. He was restarted on home medications, including tobramycin nebulizers and Esbriet, with a new nebulizer provided. He was discharged home with follow-up planned in one month for repeat bronchoscopy and continued management of chronic conditions.",
    "problems": [
      "Acute respiratory failure with hypoxia",
      "Tracheal and LMS bronchus stenosis",
      "Relapsing polychondritis",
      "Elevated white blood cell count, unspecified",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Chronic pseudomonal colonization",
      "Malfunction of tracheostomy stoma"
    ]
  }
}
